<title>ITALY: SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scorers in Italian first</p>
<p>division after matches on Sunday:</p>
<p>11 - Filippo Inzaghi (Atalanta)</p>
<p>9 - Abel Balbo (Roma)</p>
<p>8 - Pasquale Luiso (Piacenza)</p>
<p>7 - Gabriel Batistuta (Fiorentina), Roberto Mancini and</p>
<p>Vincenzo Montella (both Sampdoria), Marcello Otero (Vicenza),</p>
<p>George Weah (Milan)</p>
<p>6 - Oliver Bierhoff (Udinese), Youri Djorkaeff (Inter), Igor</p>
<p>Kolyvanov (Bologna), Giuseppe Signori (Lazio)</p>
<p>5 - Alfredo Aglietti (Napoli), Enrico Chiesa (Parma),</p>
<p>Alessandro Del Piero (Juventus), Filippo Maniero (Verona), Paolo</p>
<p>Poggi (Udinese), Luis Oliveira (Fiorentina)</p>
<p>4 - Demetrio Albertini and Roberto Baggio (both Milan), Nicola</p>
<p>Caccia and Andrea Cruz (both Napoli), Carmine Gautieri</p>
<p>(Perugia), Giampiero Maini (Vicenza),  Roberto Muzzi and Sandro</p>
<p>Tovalieri (both Cagliari), Michele Padovano (Juventus)</p>
</text>
